,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2909900850,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyOTA5OTAwODUw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:export","name":"topic:export","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2025-10-23T08:40:02Z","updated_at":"2025-10-23T08:58:05Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.5 stable.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200)\n\n### Issue description\n\nOne-click deploy (Remote deploy) doesn't work when remote user has \" \" in their user folder.\nFor example, user named as ```jack smith``` typically will have user folder like \"C:\\Users\\jack smith\"\n\nWe can see `\"$action = New-ScheduledTaskAction -Execute 'C:\\Users\\jack smith\\\\{exe_name}' -Argument '{cmd_args}'\" `\n\nwill create a schedule that points to \"C:\\Users\\jack\" with \"smith\\\\{exe_name}\" as args.\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/5950fca36cb311edcc72e479effed5c477d20adb/platform/windows/export/export_plugin.cpp#L483\n\nAnd this scheduled task action will fail without giving any error.\n\n```\nStopping and deleting previous version...\nCreating temporary directory...\nUploading archive...\nUploading scripts...\nStarting project...\nProject started.\n```\n\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a local user with \" \" in username and make sure user folder also have that \" \".\nOne-click deploy to that user.\nYou can see new folder in %TEMP% was created but never be executed.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https